## Echora Contribution & Distribution Addendum

This addendum supplements, and does not replace, the PolyForm Strict
License 1.0.0 above. Where this addendum grants a permission, that
permission is limited exactly as stated here; every other term and
restriction of the License above remains in full force.

1. **End-User Use.** Running an official, unmodified release of the
   Software published by the Licensor (for example, via the official
   GitHub repository's Releases) is use for a permitted purpose under the
   License's "Personal Uses" and "Noncommercial Purposes" clauses, and is
   expressly confirmed as permitted.

2. **Contribution Forks.** You may create a fork of the Software's source
   code, and make changes to that fork, solely to prepare and submit a
   contribution (such as a pull request, patch, or bug report with a
   fix) to the Licensor's official repository. Such a fork must not be
   published, promoted, advertised, or kept available to the public or
   any third party for any purpose other than that submission, and must
   be deleted or made private once the contribution process concludes,
   whether or not the contribution is accepted.

3. **Contribution License Grant.** By submitting a contribution to the
   Licensor's official repository, you grant the Licensor a perpetual,
   worldwide, royalty-free, irrevocable license to use, reproduce,
   modify, and incorporate that contribution into the Software under
   these terms (or any future license the Licensor chooses for the
   Software), and you represent that you have the right to grant this
   license.

4. **No Other Rights.** Nothing in this addendum grants any right to
   distribute, sell, sublicense, publish, or otherwise make the Software,
   or any modified version of it, available to any third party, except
   as strictly necessary to submit a contribution under Section 2.

